IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`

-- coa26-ch2b.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 42, Chapter 2 (Individuals and firms), ss 1217 to 1222:
-- supervisory bodies, exemption from liability for damages, professional qualifications, third country
-- qualifications, and individuals retaining only a 1967 Act authorisation. Lines 17115-17214 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- (ss 1212-1216 are in coa26-ch2a.l4, which imports this module.)
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa26-ch1.l4 (MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words,
-- each such branch with a FALSE-kind comment; NOTHING otherwise, each branch with a NOTHING-kind comment).
-- Seams: "recognised" (Schedules 10 and 11, coa30), "quoted company" (s 385, coa8) and "third country" questions are INPUTS.

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Individuals and firms`

§§§ `Supervisory bodies (ss 1217-1218)`

-- ---- s 1217: Supervisory bodies ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17117 | (1) In this Part a “supervisory body” means a body established in the United Kingdom (whether a body corporate or an unincorporated association) which maintains and enforces rules as to—
-- src:17118 | (a) the eligibility of persons for appointment as a statutory auditor, and
-- src:17119 | (b) the conduct of statutory audit work,
-- src:17120 | which are binding on persons seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor . . . because they are members of that body . . . .
@ref s 1217(1) "supervisory body" (src:17117-17120)
GIVEN `the body is established in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body corporate or an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body maintains and enforces rules as to the eligibility of persons for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body maintains and enforces rules as to the conduct of statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those rules are binding on persons seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor because they are members of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1217(1) the body is a supervisory body` MEANS
    IF     `the body is established in the United Kingdom`
       AND `the body is a body corporate or an unincorporated association`
       AND `the body maintains and enforces rules as to the eligibility of persons for appointment as a statutory auditor`
       AND `the body maintains and enforces rules as to the conduct of statutory audit work`
       AND `those rules are binding on persons seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor because they are members of the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part a “supervisory body” means a body established in the United Kingdom"

-- src:17121 | (1A) The rules referred to in paragraphs 9(1A) and 10C(3) (bar on appointment as director or other officer), paragraph 9(3)(b) (confidentiality of information) and paragraph 12(3)(b)(v) (temporary prohibition from exercising functions in a firm) of Schedule 10 must also be binding on persons who—
-- src:17122 | (a) have sought appointment or acted as a statutory auditor, and
-- src:17123 | (b) have been members of the body at any time after the commencement of this Part.
@ref s 1217(1A) Rules that must also be binding (src:17121-17123)
GIVEN `the person has sought appointment or acted as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been a member of the body at any time after the commencement of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1217(1A) the specified rules of Schedule 10 must also be binding on the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person has sought appointment or acted as a statutory auditor`
       AND `the person has been a member of the body at any time after the commencement of Part 42`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must also be binding on persons who— (a) have sought appointment or acted as a statutory auditor, and (b) have been members of the body"

-- src:17124 | (2) In this Part references to the members of a supervisory body are to the persons who, whether or not members of the body, are subject to its rules in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1217(2) Members of a supervisory body (src:17124)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the rules of the body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1217(2) the person is a member of the supervisory body` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the rules of the body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to the members of a supervisory body are to the persons who, whether or not members of the body, are subject to its rules"

-- src:17125 | (3) In this Part references to the rules of a supervisory body are to the rules (whether or not laid down by the body itself) which the body or the competent authority has power to enforce and which are relevant for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 1217(3) Rules of a supervisory body (src:17125)
GIVEN `the body or the competent authority has power to enforce the rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1217(3) the rule is a rule of the supervisory body` MEANS
    -- whether or not laid down by the body itself makes no difference
    IF     `the body or the competent authority has power to enforce the rule`
       AND `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to the rules of a supervisory body are to the rules (whether or not laid down by the body itself) which the body or the competent authority has power to enforce and which are relevant for the purposes of this Part"

-- src:17126 | This includes rules relating to the admission or expulsion of members of the body, so far as relevant for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 1217(3) Rules relating to the admission or expulsion of members (src:17126)
GIVEN `the rule relates to the admission or expulsion of members of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1217(3) the rule on admission or expulsion is included among the rules of the supervisory body` MEANS
    IF     `the rule relates to the admission or expulsion of members of the body`
       AND `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "This includes rules relating to the admission or expulsion of members of the body, so far as relevant"

-- src:17127 | (4) Schedule 10 has effect with respect to the recognition of supervisory bodies for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 1217(4) Schedule 10: recognition of supervisory bodies (src:17127)
GIVEN `sch 10 recognised supervisory bodies: the body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1217(4) the supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body for the purposes of Part 42` MEANS
    -- Schedule 10 (coa30) decides; the answer passes straight through.
    CONSIDER `sch 10 recognised supervisory bodies: the body is a recognised supervisory body`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Schedule 10 has effect with respect to the recognition of supervisory bodies" (the definition is handed to Schedule 10, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 10 is another part's range

-- ---- s 1218: Exemption from liability for damages ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17130 | (2) The persons within this subsection are—
-- src:17131 | (a) any recognised supervisory body,
-- src:17132 | (b) any officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body, and
-- src:17133 | (c) any member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body.
@ref s 1218(2) The persons exempt from liability (src:17130-17133)
GIVEN `the person is a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1218(2) the person is within subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a recognised supervisory body`
        OR `the person is an officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body`
        OR `the person is a member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons within this subsection are— (a) any recognised supervisory body, (b) any officer or employee of a recognised supervisory body, and (c) any member of the governing body of a recognised supervisory body." (a list closed by "are", read as the keel reads "are": a lawyer's reading)

-- src:17134 | (3) Subsection (1) applies to the functions of a recognised supervisory body so far as relating to, or to matters arising out of, any of the following—
-- src:17135 | (a) rules, practices, powers and arrangements of the body to which the requirements of Part 2 of Schedule 10 apply;
-- src:17136 | (b) the obligations with which paragraph 20 of that Schedule requires the body to comply;
-- src:17137 | (c) any guidance issued by the body;
-- src:17138 | (d) the obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of this Part or by or by virtue of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016;
-- src:17139 | (e) the obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of the Audit Regulation.
@ref s 1218(3) The functions to which subsection (1) applies (src:17134-17139)
GIVEN `the function relates to rules, practices, powers and arrangements of the body to which the requirements of Part 2 of Schedule 10 apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function relates to the obligations with which paragraph 20 of Schedule 10 requires the body to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function relates to any guidance issued by the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function relates to the obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of Part 42 or the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function relates to the obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of the Audit Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1218(3) subsection (1) applies to the function of the recognised supervisory body` MEANS
    -- "so far as relating to, or to matters arising out of, any of the following": the list limits the grant
    IF     `the function relates to rules, practices, powers and arrangements of the body to which the requirements of Part 2 of Schedule 10 apply`
        OR `the function relates to the obligations with which paragraph 20 of Schedule 10 requires the body to comply`
        OR `the function relates to any guidance issued by the body`
        OR `the function relates to the obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of Part 42 or the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016`
        OR `the function relates to the obligations imposed on the body by or by virtue of the Audit Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) applies to the functions of a recognised supervisory body so far as relating to, or to matters arising out of, any of the following"

-- src:17140 | (4) The reference in subsection (3)(c) to guidance issued by a recognised supervisory body is a reference to any guidance or recommendation which is—
-- src:17141 | (a) issued or made by it to all or any class of its members or persons seeking to become members, and
-- src:17142 | (b) relevant for the purposes of this Part , the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation,
@ref s 1218(4) Guidance issued by a recognised supervisory body (src:17140-17142)
GIVEN `the guidance or recommendation is issued or made by the body to all or any class of its members or persons seeking to become members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance or recommendation is relevant for the purposes of Part 42, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1218(4) the guidance is guidance issued by the recognised supervisory body` MEANS
    IF     `the guidance or recommendation is issued or made by the body to all or any class of its members or persons seeking to become members`
       AND `the guidance or recommendation is relevant for the purposes of Part 42, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a reference to any guidance or recommendation which is— (a) issued or made by it to all or any class of its members or persons seeking to become members, and (b) relevant for the purposes of this Part"

-- src:17143 | including any guidance or recommendation relating to the admission or expulsion of members of the body, so far as relevant for the purposes of this Part , the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation.
@ref s 1218(4) Guidance on the admission or expulsion of members (src:17143)
GIVEN `the guidance or recommendation relates to the admission or expulsion of members of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance or recommendation is relevant for the purposes of Part 42, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1218(4) the guidance on admission or expulsion is included as guidance issued by the recognised supervisory body` MEANS
    IF     `the guidance or recommendation relates to the admission or expulsion of members of the body`
       AND `the guidance or recommendation is relevant for the purposes of Part 42, the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or the Audit Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including any guidance or recommendation relating to the admission or expulsion of members of the body, so far as relevant"

-- src:17144 | (5) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:17145 | (a) if the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith, or
-- src:17146 | (b) so as to prevent an award of damages in respect of the act or omission on the ground that it was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998 (c. 42) (acts of public authorities incompatible with Convention rights).
@ref s 1218(5) Subsection (1) does not apply (src:17144-17146)
GIVEN `the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award of damages would be on the ground that the act or omission was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1218(5) subsection (1) does not apply to the act or omission` MEANS
    IF     `the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith`
        OR `the award of damages would be on the ground that the act or omission was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(5) Subsection (1) does not apply— (a) if the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith" (a failed "if", a lawyer's reading)

-- src:17129 | (1) No person within subsection (2) is to be liable in damages for anything done or omitted in the discharge or purported discharge of functions to which this subsection applies.
@ref s 1218(1) No liability in damages (src:17129)
GIVEN `the person is within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the function is one to which subsection (1) applies by subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply by subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1218(1) the person is liable in damages for anything done or omitted in the discharge or purported discharge of the function` MEANS
    -- This section only ever says "no": it never makes anyone liable. Where its limits are not met, liability is left to the general law.
    IF     `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the person is within subsection (2)`
       AND `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the function is one to which subsection (1) applies by subsection (3)`
       AND `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` `subsection (1) does not apply by subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person within subsection (2) is to be liable in damages for anything done or omitted in the discharge or purported discharge of functions to which this subsection applies."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption reaches only persons within subsection (2), functions within subsection (3), and not the cases in subsection (5)

§§§ `Professional qualifications (ss 1219-1222)`

-- ---- s 1219: Appropriate qualifications ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:17160 | (2) A person is within this subsection if—
-- src:17161 | (a) before 1st January 1990, he began a course of study or practical training leading to a professional qualification in accountancy offered by a body established in the United Kingdom,
-- src:17162 | (b) he obtained that qualification on or after 1st January 1990 and before 1st January 1996, and
-- src:17163 | (c) the Secretary of State approved his qualification before 1st October 2018 as an appropriate qualification for the purposes of this Chapter.
@ref s 1219(2) The persons within this subsection (src:17160-17163)
GIVEN `the date the person began a course of study or practical training leading to the qualification` IS A DATE
      `the qualification is a professional qualification in accountancy offered by a body established in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person obtained the qualification` IS A DATE
      `the date the Secretary of State approved the qualification as an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42, if he did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1219(2) the person is within this subsection` MEANS
    IF     `the date the person began a course of study or practical training leading to the qualification` LESS THAN (Date 1 1 1990)
       AND `the qualification is a professional qualification in accountancy offered by a body established in the United Kingdom`
       AND `the date the person obtained the qualification` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1990)
       AND `the date the person obtained the qualification` LESS THAN (Date 1 1 1996)
       AND `approval before 1st October 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is within this subsection if— (a) before 1st January 1990, he began a course ... (b) he obtained that qualification on or after 1st January 1990 and before 1st January 1996, and (c) the Secretary of State approved his qualification before 1st October 2018"
    WHERE
        `approval before 1st October 2018` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the Secretary of State approved the qualification as an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42, if he did`
            WHEN JUST d THEN d LESS THAN (Date 1 10 2018)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 1219(1)(e) and (3) are blank in this text (coverage: repealed or blank).
-- src:17149 | (1) A person holds an appropriate qualification for the purposes of this Chapter if and only if—
-- src:17150 | (a) he holds a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom,
-- src:17151 | (b) immediately before the commencement of this Chapter, he—
-- src:17152 | (i) held an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part 2 of the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40) (eligibility for appointment as company auditor) by virtue of section 31(1)(a) or (c) of that Act, or
-- src:17153 | (ii) was treated as holding an appropriate qualification for those purposes by virtue of section 31(2), (3) or (4) of that Act,
-- src:17154 | (c) immediately before the commencement of this Chapter, he—
-- src:17155 | (i) held an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part III of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 (S.I. 1990/593 (N.I. 5)) by virtue of Article 34(1)(a) or (c) of that Order, or
-- src:17156 | (ii) was treated as holding an appropriate qualification for those purposes by virtue of Article 34(2), (3) or (4) of that Order,
-- src:17157 | (d) he is within subsection (2), or
-- src:17158 | (e) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:17159 | (f) subject to any direction under section 1221(5), he is regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as holding an approved third country qualification.
@ref s 1219(1) Appropriate qualifications (src:17149-17159)
GIVEN `the person holds a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 11 recognised professional qualifications: the person's qualification is a recognised professional qualification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person held an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part 2 of the Companies Act 1989 by virtue of section 31(1)(a) or (c) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person was treated as holding an appropriate qualification for those purposes by virtue of section 31(2), (3) or (4) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person held an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part III of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 by virtue of Article 34(1)(a) or (c) of that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person was treated as holding an appropriate qualification for those purposes by virtue of Article 34(2), (3) or (4) of that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is regarded for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42 as holding an approved third country qualification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a direction under section 1221(5) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the additional educational qualifications that direction specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1219(1) the person holds an appropriate qualification` MEANS
    `coa26 support any of the answers` `the limbs of subsection (1)`
    WHERE
        `the limbs of subsection (1)` MEANS
            LIST `limb (a) a recognised qualification obtained in the United Kingdom`
               , JUST (  `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person held an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part 2 of the Companies Act 1989 by virtue of section 31(1)(a) or (c) of that Act`
                      OR `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person was treated as holding an appropriate qualification for those purposes by virtue of section 31(2), (3) or (4) of that Act`)  -- (b)
               , JUST (  `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person held an appropriate qualification for the purposes of Part III of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 by virtue of Article 34(1)(a) or (c) of that Order`
                      OR `immediately before the commencement of Chapter 2 of Part 42 the person was treated as holding an appropriate qualification for those purposes by virtue of Article 34(2), (3) or (4) of that Order`)  -- (c)
               , `the person is within subsection (2)`                                                      -- (d)
               , `limb (f) an approved third country qualification`                                         -- (f)
        `limb (a) a recognised qualification obtained in the United Kingdom` MEANS
            IF `the person holds a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom`
            THEN `sch 11 recognised professional qualifications: the person's qualification is a recognised professional qualification`
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if and only if— (a) he holds a recognised professional qualification obtained in the United Kingdom"
        `limb (f) an approved third country qualification` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the person is regarded for the purposes of Chapter 2 of Part 42 as holding an approved third country qualification`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                IF `a direction under section 1221(5) applies to the person` AND (NOT `the person holds the additional educational qualifications that direction specifies`)
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to any direction under section 1221(5)"
                ELSE JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if and only if— ... (f) ... he is regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as holding an approved third country qualification"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a declaration under section 1221(1) covers the person is not known
    -- JUST FALSE only when every limb is JUST FALSE ("if and only if"); NOTHING when a borrowed answer (Schedule 11, section 1221) is not known.
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person holds an appropriate qualification for the purposes of this Chapter if and only if—"

-- ---- s 1220: Qualifying bodies and recognised professional qualifications --------------------------------

-- src:17166 | (1) In this Part a “qualifying body” means a body established in the United Kingdom (whether a body corporate or an unincorporated association) which offers a professional qualification in accountancy.
@ref s 1220(1) "qualifying body" (src:17166)
GIVEN `the body is established in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body corporate or an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body offers a professional qualification in accountancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1220(1) the body is a qualifying body` MEANS
    IF     `the body is established in the United Kingdom`
       AND `the body is a body corporate or an unincorporated association`
       AND `the body offers a professional qualification in accountancy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part a “qualifying body” means a body established in the United Kingdom"

-- src:17167 | (2) In this Part references to the rules of a qualifying body are to the rules (whether or not laid down by the body itself) which the body has power to enforce and which are relevant for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 1220(2) Rules of a qualifying body (src:17167)
GIVEN `the body has power to enforce the rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1220(2) the rule is a rule of the qualifying body` MEANS
    IF     `the body has power to enforce the rule`
       AND `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to the rules of a qualifying body are to the rules (whether or not laid down by the body itself) which the body has power to enforce and which are relevant for the purposes of this Part"

-- src:17168 | This includes, so far as so relevant, rules relating to—
-- src:17169 | (a) admission to or expulsion from a course of study leading to a qualification,
-- src:17170 | (b) the award or deprivation of a qualification, or
-- src:17171 | (c) the approval of a person for the purposes of giving practical training or the withdrawal of such approval.
@ref s 1220(2) Rules relating to admission, award or approval (src:17168-17171)
GIVEN `the rule relates to admission to or expulsion from a course of study leading to a qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule relates to the award or deprivation of a qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule relates to the approval of a person for the purposes of giving practical training or the withdrawal of such approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1220(2) the rule is included among the rules of the qualifying body` MEANS
    IF     `the rule is relevant for the purposes of Part 42`
       AND (   `the rule relates to admission to or expulsion from a course of study leading to a qualification`
            OR `the rule relates to the award or deprivation of a qualification`
            OR `the rule relates to the approval of a person for the purposes of giving practical training or the withdrawal of such approval`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "This includes, so far as so relevant, rules relating to— (a) admission to or expulsion from a course of study"

-- src:17172 | (3) Schedule 11 has effect with respect to the recognition for the purposes of this Part of a professional qualification offered by a qualifying body.
@ref s 1220(3) Schedule 11: recognition of professional qualifications (src:17172)
GIVEN `sch 11 recognised professional qualifications: the qualification is a recognised professional qualification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1220(3) the professional qualification is a recognised professional qualification for the purposes of Part 42` MEANS
    -- Schedule 11 (coa30) decides; the answer passes straight through.
    CONSIDER `sch 11 recognised professional qualifications: the qualification is a recognised professional qualification`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Schedule 11 has effect with respect to the recognition for the purposes of this Part of a professional qualification offered by a qualifying body" (handed to Schedule 11, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 11 is another part's range

-- ---- s 1221: Approval of third country qualifications ---------------------------------------------------
-- s 1221(7B) and (9) are blank in this text (coverage: repealed or blank).

-- src:17187 | (3) The Secretary of State may make a declaration under subsection (1) only if he is satisfied that—
-- src:17188 | (a) in the case of a declaration under subsection (1)(a), the fact that the persons in question are qualified to audit accounts under the law of the specified third country, taken with any requirement or requirements to be specified under subsection (1A), or
-- src:17189 | (b) in the case of a declaration under subsection (1)(b), the specified professional qualification taken with any requirement or requirements to be specified under subsections (1A) or (2),
-- src:17190 | affords an assurance of professional competence equivalent to that afforded by a recognised professional qualification.
@ref s 1221(3) Condition for a declaration: equivalent assurance of professional competence (src:17187-17190)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the fact or the qualification, taken with any requirement specified, affords an assurance of professional competence equivalent to that afforded by a recognised professional qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(3) the condition for making a declaration under subsection (1) is met` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the fact or the qualification, taken with any requirement specified, affords an assurance of professional competence equivalent to that afforded by a recognised professional qualification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may make a declaration under subsection (1) only if he is satisfied that"

-- src:17191 | (4) The Secretary of State may make a declaration under subsection (1) only if he is satisfied that the treatment that the persons who are the subject of the declaration will receive as a result of it is comparable to the treatment which is, or is likely to be, afforded in the specified third country or a part of it to—
-- src:17192 | (a) in the case of a declaration under subsection (1)(a), some or all persons who are eligible to be appointed as a statutory auditor, and
-- src:17193 | (b) in the case of a declaration under subsection (1)(b), some or all persons who hold a corresponding recognised professional qualification.
@ref s 1221(4) Condition for a declaration: comparable treatment (src:17191-17193)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the treatment the persons will receive as a result of the declaration is comparable to the treatment afforded in the specified third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(4) the condition for making a declaration under subsection (1) is met` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the treatment the persons will receive as a result of the declaration is comparable to the treatment afforded in the specified third country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may make a declaration under subsection (1) only if he is satisfied that the treatment"

-- src:17174 | (1) The Secretary of State may declare that the following are to be regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as holding an approved third country qualification—
-- src:17175 | (a) persons who are qualified to audit accounts under the law of a specified third country, or
-- src:17176 | (b) persons who hold a specified professional qualification in accountancy obtained in a specified third country.
@ref s 1221(1) Declaration that persons hold an approved third country qualification (src:17174-17176)
GIVEN `the persons are qualified to audit accounts under the law of a specified third country, or hold a specified professional qualification in accountancy obtained in a specified third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in subsection (3) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition in subsection (4) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(1) the Secretary of State may declare that the persons are regarded as holding an approved third country qualification` MEANS
    IF NOT `the persons are qualified to audit accounts under the law of a specified third country, or hold a specified professional qualification in accountancy obtained in a specified third country`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is limited to persons within paragraph (a) or (b)
    ELSE `coa26 support both answers` `the condition in subsection (3) is met` `the condition in subsection (4) is met`
    -- JUST TRUE when both conditions are met; JUST FALSE when either is not met
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if he is satisfied that" (subsections (3) and (4))

-- src:17177 | (1A) A declaration under subsection (1)(a) or (b) must contain provision to the effect that a person is not to be regarded as holding an approved third country qualification for the purposes of this Chapter unless the person—
-- src:17178 | (a) already holds a professional qualification which—
-- src:17179 | (i) covers subjects and skills which are the same or substantially the same as the subjects and skills that are covered by a recognised professional qualification, where the knowledge of those subjects and skills is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor, and
-- src:17180 | (ii) demonstrates knowledge of those subjects and skills to the same or substantially the same standard as that demonstrated by the recognised professional qualification, or
-- src:17181 | (b) holds a professional qualification which does not comply with paragraph (a) and has met whichever of the requirements of subsection (1B) as is specified in the declaration.
@ref s 1221(1A) A declaration must contain provision as to what a person must hold (src:17177-17181)
GIVEN `the person already holds a professional qualification which covers subjects and skills the same or substantially the same as those covered by a recognised professional qualification, knowledge of which is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that qualification demonstrates knowledge of those subjects and skills to the same or substantially the same standard as the recognised professional qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a professional qualification which does not comply with paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has met the requirement of subsection (1B) specified in the declaration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(1A) the person may be regarded as holding an approved third country qualification` MEANS
    -- "unless": a necessary condition. JUST FALSE when neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) is satisfied; otherwise NOTHING,
    -- because the subsection only says what the declaration must contain, not that the person is regarded as holding the qualification.
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` (`coa26 support either answer` `paragraph (a) holds` `paragraph (b) holds`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is not to be regarded as holding an approved third country qualification for the purposes of this Chapter unless the person"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" states a necessary condition only; the declaration under subsection (1) decides whether the person is regarded as holding the qualification
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS JUST (`the person already holds a professional qualification which covers subjects and skills the same or substantially the same as those covered by a recognised professional qualification, knowledge of which is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` AND `that qualification demonstrates knowledge of those subjects and skills to the same or substantially the same standard as the recognised professional qualification`)
        `paragraph (b) holds` MEANS
            IF `the person holds a professional qualification which does not comply with paragraph (a)`
            THEN `the person has met the requirement of subsection (1B) specified in the declaration`
            ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `s 1221(1B) way the declaration specifies that the condition is satisfied` IS ONE OF
    `s 1221(1B)(a) only by passing an aptitude test`
    `s 1221(1B)(b) only by completing an adaptation period`
    `s 1221(1B)(c) either by passing an aptitude test or by completing an adaptation period`

-- src:17182 | (1B) The declaration must specify that the condition in subsection (1A)(b) is satisfied in one of the following ways—
-- src:17183 | (a) only by passing an aptitude test in accordance with subsection (7A),
-- src:17184 | (b) only by completing an adaptation period in accordance with subsections (7C) and (7D), or
-- src:17185 | (c) either by passing an aptitude test in accordance with subsection (7A) or by completing an adaptation period in accordance with subsections (7C) and (7D), according to the choice of the person.
@ref s 1221(1B) How the condition in subsection (1A)(b) is satisfied (src:17182-17185)
GIVEN way IS A `s 1221(1B) way the declaration specifies that the condition is satisfied`
      `the person has passed an aptitude test in accordance with subsection (7A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has completed an adaptation period in accordance with subsections (7C) and (7D)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(1B) the person has met the requirement the declaration specifies` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 1221(1B)(a) only by passing an aptitude test` THEN
        IF `the person has passed an aptitude test in accordance with subsection (7A)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) only by passing an aptitude test in accordance with subsection (7A)"
    WHEN `s 1221(1B)(b) only by completing an adaptation period` THEN
        IF `the person has completed an adaptation period in accordance with subsections (7C) and (7D)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) only by completing an adaptation period in accordance with subsections (7C) and (7D)"
    WHEN `s 1221(1B)(c) either by passing an aptitude test or by completing an adaptation period` THEN
        IF `the person has passed an aptitude test in accordance with subsection (7A)` OR `the person has completed an adaptation period in accordance with subsections (7C) and (7D)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) either by passing an aptitude test ... or by completing an adaptation period ... according to the choice of the person"

-- src:17186 | (2) A declaration under subsection (1)(b) may be expressed to be subject to the satisfaction of any specified requirement or requirements.
@ref s 1221(2) A declaration under subsection (1)(b) may be subject to requirements (src:17186)
GIVEN `the declaration is under subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(2) the declaration may be expressed to be subject to the satisfaction of the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the declaration is under subsection (1)(b)` AND `the requirement is specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A declaration under subsection (1)(b) may be expressed to be subject to the satisfaction of any specified requirement"

-- src:17194 | (5) The Secretary of State may direct that persons holding an approved third country qualification are not to be treated as holding an appropriate qualification for the purposes of this Chapter unless they hold such additional educational qualifications as the Secretary of State may specify for the purpose of ensuring that such persons have an adequate knowledge of the law and practice in the United Kingdom relevant to the audit of accounts.
@ref s 1221(5) Directions as to additional educational qualifications (src:17194)
GIVEN `the persons hold an approved third country qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional educational qualifications are specified for the purpose of ensuring that the persons have an adequate knowledge of the law and practice in the United Kingdom relevant to the audit of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(5) the Secretary of State may direct that the persons are not treated as holding an appropriate qualification unless they hold the additional educational qualifications` MEANS
    IF     `the persons hold an approved third country qualification`
       AND `the additional educational qualifications are specified for the purpose of ensuring that the persons have an adequate knowledge of the law and practice in the United Kingdom relevant to the audit of accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to direct about "persons holding an approved third country qualification" and for the stated purpose

-- src:17195 | (6) The Secretary of State may give different directions in relation to different approved third country qualifications.
@ref s 1221(6) Different directions (src:17195)
GIVEN `the directions are given in relation to different approved third country qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(6) the Secretary of State may give different directions` MEANS
    IF `the directions are given in relation to different approved third country qualifications`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "different directions in relation to different approved third country qualifications"

-- src:17196 | (7) The Secretary of State may, if he thinks fit, having regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4), withdraw a declaration under subsection (1) in relation to—
-- src:17197 | (a) persons becoming qualified to audit accounts under the law of the specified third country after such date as he may specify, or
-- src:17198 | (b) persons obtaining the specified professional qualification after such date as he may specify.
@ref s 1221(7) Withdrawal of a declaration (src:17196-17198)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the withdrawal is in relation to persons qualified or qualifying after the date he specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(7) the Secretary of State may withdraw a declaration under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State thinks fit`
       AND `the Secretary of State has regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4)`
       AND `the withdrawal is in relation to persons qualified or qualifying after the date he specifies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he thinks fit, having regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4), withdraw a declaration under subsection (1) in relation to— (a) persons becoming qualified ... after such date as he may specify"

DECLARE `s 1221(7A) matter the aptitude test may cover` IS ONE OF
    `s 1221(7A)(a) the person's knowledge of required subjects and skills`
    `s 1221(7A)(b) the person's knowledge of rules of professional conduct`
    `s 1221(7A)(c) the person's knowledge of any other matters`

DECLARE `s 1221(7A) status of a matter in the aptitude test` IS ONE OF
    `s 1221(7A) the test must cover it`
    `s 1221(7A) the test may cover it`
    `s 1221(7A) the test must not cover it`

-- src:17199 | (7A) An aptitude test required for the purposes of subsection (1B) —
-- src:17200 | (a) must test the person’s knowledge of required subjects and skills,
-- src:17201 | (b) may test the person's knowledge of rules of professional conduct;
-- src:17202 | (c) must not test the person's knowledge of any other matters.
@ref s 1221(7A) The aptitude test (src:17199-17202)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 1221(7A) matter the aptitude test may cover`
GIVETH A `s 1221(7A) status of a matter in the aptitude test`
`s 1221(7A) the status of the matter in an aptitude test required for the purposes of subsection (1B)` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 1221(7A)(a) the person's knowledge of required subjects and skills` THEN `s 1221(7A) the test must cover it` -- "must test"
    WHEN `s 1221(7A)(b) the person's knowledge of rules of professional conduct` THEN `s 1221(7A) the test may cover it` -- "may test"
    WHEN `s 1221(7A)(c) the person's knowledge of any other matters` THEN `s 1221(7A) the test must not cover it` -- "must not test"

-- src:17203 | (7AA) For the purposes of subsection (7A), a subject or skill is a required subject or skill if it is covered by a recognised professional qualification and knowledge of it is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor, but—
-- src:17204 | (a) the professional qualification already held by the person (“the existing qualification”) does not cover the same or substantially the same subject or skill, or
-- src:17205 | (b) the existing qualification does not demonstrate knowledge of that subject or skill to the same or substantially the same standard as that demonstrated by the recognised professional qualification.
@ref s 1221(7AA) A required subject or skill (src:17203-17205)
GIVEN `the subject or skill is covered by a recognised professional qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowledge of it is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualification already held does not cover the same or substantially the same subject or skill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualification already held does not demonstrate knowledge of that subject or skill to the same or substantially the same standard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(7AA) the subject or skill is a required subject or skill` MEANS
    IF     `the subject or skill is covered by a recognised professional qualification`
       AND `knowledge of it is essential for the pursuit of the profession of statutory auditor`
       AND (   `the qualification already held does not cover the same or substantially the same subject or skill`
            OR `the qualification already held does not demonstrate knowledge of that subject or skill to the same or substantially the same standard`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a subject or skill is a required subject or skill if it is covered by a recognised professional qualification and knowledge of it is essential ... but— (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:17207 | (7C) An adaptation period is a period, not exceeding three years, in which the person (“the applicant”) pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of another person who holds an appropriate qualification, subject to an assessment (“the ability assessment”) of the applicant’s ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1221(7C) Adaptation period (src:17207)
GIVEN `the length of the period in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicant pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of another person who holds an appropriate qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pursuit is subject to an assessment of the applicant's ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(7C) the period is an adaptation period` MEANS
    IF     `the length of the period in months` AT MOST 36 -- "not exceeding three years"
       AND `the applicant pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of another person who holds an appropriate qualification`
       AND `the pursuit is subject to an assessment of the applicant's ability to pursue the profession of statutory auditor in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An adaptation period is a period, not exceeding three years, in which the person (“the applicant”) pursues the profession of statutory auditor under the supervision of another person who holds an appropriate qualification, subject to an assessment"

-- src:17208 | (7D) The adaptation period must be completed, and the ability assessment must be carried out, in accordance with the rules and practices of a recognised supervisory body (see paragraph 7A of Schedule 10).
@ref s 1221(7D) How the adaptation period must be completed (src:17208)
GIVEN `the adaptation period has been completed in accordance with the rules and practices of the supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ability assessment has been carried out in accordance with the rules and practices of the supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 10 para 7A the supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(7D) the adaptation period and the ability assessment accord with subsection (7D)` MEANS
    IF     `the adaptation period has been completed in accordance with the rules and practices of the supervisory body`
       AND `the ability assessment has been carried out in accordance with the rules and practices of the supervisory body`
    THEN `sch 10 para 7A the supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The adaptation period must be completed, and the ability assessment must be carried out, in accordance with the rules and practices of a recognised supervisory body" (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17209 | (8) The Secretary of State may, if he thinks fit, having regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4), vary or revoke a requirement specified under subsection (2) from such date as he may specify.
@ref s 1221(8) Variation or revocation of a requirement (src:17209)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement was specified under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1221(8) the Secretary of State may vary or revoke the requirement` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State thinks fit`
       AND `the Secretary of State has regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4)`
       AND `the requirement was specified under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he thinks fit, having regard to the considerations mentioned in subsections (3) and (4), vary or revoke a requirement specified under subsection (2)"

-- ---- s 1222: Eligibility of individuals retaining only 1967 Act authorisation -----------------------

-- src:17213 | (2) A company is “unquoted” if, at the time of the person's appointment, neither the company, nor any parent undertaking of which it is a subsidiary undertaking, is a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2).
@ref s 1222(2) "unquoted" (src:17213)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2) at the time of the person's appointment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 385 each parent undertaking of which the company is a subsidiary undertaking is a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2) at that time` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1222(2) the company is unquoted` MEANS
    -- "unquoted" if neither the company nor any such parent undertaking is quoted: the opposite of "some one of them is quoted".
    -- JUST FALSE when one of them is quoted ("A company is “unquoted” if ... neither").
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is “unquoted” if, at the time of the person's appointment, neither the company, nor any parent undertaking of which it is a subsidiary undertaking, is a quoted company"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 385(2) belongs to another part, so an unknown answer there stays unknown.
    `coa26 support the opposite answer` (`coa26 support any of the answers` (`s 385 the company is a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2) at the time of the person's appointment` FOLLOWED BY `s 385 each parent undertaking of which the company is a subsidiary undertaking is a quoted company within the meaning of section 385(2) at that time`))

-- src:17212 | (1) A person whose only appropriate qualification is based on his retention of an authorisation originally granted by the Board of Trade or the Secretary of State under section 13(1) of the Companies Act 1967 (c. 81) is eligible only for appointment as auditor of an unquoted company.
@ref s 1222(1) Individuals retaining only a 1967 Act authorisation (src:17212)
GIVEN `the person's only appropriate qualification is based on his retention of an authorisation originally granted by the Board of Trade or the Secretary of State under section 13(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is unquoted` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1222(1) the person is eligible for appointment as auditor of the company` MEANS
    -- "eligible only for appointment as auditor of an unquoted company": JUST FALSE when the person is within the section and the company is not unquoted.
    IF NOT `the person's only appropriate qualification is based on his retention of an authorisation originally granted by the Board of Trade or the Secretary of State under section 13(1) of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person whose only appropriate qualification is based on his retention of an authorisation ... is eligible only for"
    ELSE IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` `the company is unquoted`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is eligible only for appointment as auditor of an unquoted company"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only for" is a limit; it does not say the person is eligible even for an unquoted company

-- src:17214 | (3) References to a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of this Part in enactments relating to eligibility for appointment as auditor of a person other than a company do not include a person to whom this section applies.
@ref s 1222(3) References in enactments about auditors of persons other than companies (src:17214)
GIVEN `the enactment relates to eligibility for appointment as auditor of a person other than a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one to whom section 1222 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1222(3) the reference to a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor includes the person` MEANS
    IF     `the enactment relates to eligibility for appointment as auditor of a person other than a company`
       AND `the person is one to whom section 1222 applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not include a person to whom this section applies"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is only for references in enactments about auditors of persons other than companies
